105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (Intensive care units \(ICU\) are specialized departments within hospitals that provide continuous care and high-level medical intervention for critically ill patients. Predicting the early mortality and sepsis is crucial for interventions, better clinical decisions, and optimal use of resources. Traditional severity scores are not able to capture the complex conditions. deep learning models can capture patterns in large quantity of clinical data typically recorded by EHR systems,)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (This work investigates different approaches to predict in-hospital mortality and sepsis based on eICU collaborative research database \(eICU-CRD\). There are two modalities present: static and time series based. LSTM and GRU are implemented to generate temporal embeddings and a denoising autoencoder for static data. Instead of treating each patient as a separate individual vector, several patients with similar conditions are grouped together and a GCN used to generate predictions on mortality and sepsis. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
